 ## Background
-The distortion loss was originally proposed in MipNeRF 360 to reduce artifacts such as floaters and background collapse in unbounded scene reconstruction [S1]. The naive $O(N^2)$ formulation was computationally prohibitive for point-based queries with high sample counts. DirectVoxGO introduced an efficient $O(N)$ implementation using prefix and suffix sums, which was subsequently adopted in frameworks like instant-nsr-pl [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. It is now a standard regularization component in differentiable volume rendering pipelines that optimize radiance fields.
+The distortion loss was originally proposed in MipNeRF 360 to reduce artifacts such as floaters and background collapse in unbounded scene reconstruction [S1]. The naive $O(N^2)$ formulation was computationally prohibitive for point-based queries with high sample counts [S2, unofficial]. DirectVoxGO introduced an efficient $O(N)$ implementation using prefix and suffix sums, which was subsequently adopted in frameworks like instant-nsr-pl [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
 
